Lol, exactly. Sometimes the cleanest first conclusion is just:

\text{something changed} \rightarrow \text{the system responded}

You do not always need the full mechanism before acknowledging the effect.

Then later, if it matters, you can reverse-engineer it: what changed, who responded, what was already latent, and which part was actual cause versus coincidence.

